    "body": "**Correction from the maker's install instructions (read 2026-11-11; local reference only):** the microARC 4 subplate **does not turn with A**. It's a BASE plate that mounts the microARC onto a fixture plate (two locating bores for 1/2 in or M12 pins, plus four counterbored holes for 5/16-18 SHCS into the plate's tapped holes) or onto the 770/1100 table T-slots. So this issue becomes **placing the 4th axis on the fixture-plate grid:**\n- a subplate fixture located on the #819 grid by its two pin bores;\n- the rotary's base and centreline are raised by the plate and subplate stack.\n- **Safety link to #804/#810:** the swing check uses the machine file's `nose_to_axis`, 10.6 in for the microARC sitting directly on the table. With a fixture plate (0.95 in) and a subplate under it, the A centreline is higher, so the tool sits closer to the rotating work than the check assumes. **`nose_to_axis` must come from the actual stack:** the machine file's value minus the plate and subplate thicknesses, or a per-setup override, before this setup is judged. Until then, **a user with a plate under the microARC must not rely on the 10.6 in figure.**",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
